@startuml
title Zenval — Atomic obligation payment
caption TARGET LOGICAL MODEL — values in trusted memory; private persistence encrypted
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty methods
autonumber
actor User
participant "HTTP controller" as HTTP
participant "RecordObligationPaymentHandler" as H
participant "AuthorizationPort" as AUTH
participant "UnitOfWork" as UOW
participant "IdempotencyStore" as IDEM
participant "ObligationRepository" as R
participant "Obligation aggregate" as O
participant "LedgerPostingPort / Ledger application" as L
participant "OutboxPort" as OUT
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
User -> HTTP : Record an actual payment + idempotency key
HTTP -> H : validated command + authenticated ActorContext
H -> AUTH : assertAllowed(actor, workspace, obligation)
AUTH --> H : allowed or reject before mutation
H -> UOW : execute(workspaceId)
UOW -> DB : BEGIN
H -> IDEM : claimOrReplay(actor/scope/key, requestHash, tx)
IDEM -> DB : workspace-scoped unique claim
alt same request already committed
  IDEM --> H : stored response
  H -> UOW : finish replay without new writes
  UOW -> DB : COMMIT
else new request
  H -> R : find(workspaceId, obligationId, tx)
  R --> H : aggregate + expectedVersion
  H -> O : allocate principal/interest/fee/tax by approved policy
  O --> H : allocation + updated state
  H -> L : post balanced event(command, same tx)
  L -> DB : persist Ledger facts after domain validation
  L --> H : businessEventId
  H -> R : save(updated obligation, expectedVersion, eventId, tx)
  R -> DB : optimistic concurrency update
  H -> OUT : append minimal versioned events(tx)
  OUT -> DB : INSERT outbox_event
  H -> IDEM : save response(tx)
  IDEM -> DB : persist idempotency result
  H -> UOW : complete
  UOW -> DB : COMMIT
end
H --> HTTP : committed result or replay
HTTP --> User : response
note over H,DB
  Any failure/conflicting key/version: ROLLBACK, no partial facts or outbox.
  Ledger application alone writes posted facts, including within this transaction.
  Principal is not expense; fees/interest follow direction/policy.
  This records a payment fact; it never initiates a bank payment.
  Handler names and transaction APIs are proposed contracts.
end note
@enduml
